    "case_id": "490",
    "case_summary": "A 34-year-old Palestinian prisoner was admitted to the hospital on day 33 of an organized hunger strike, with a one-week history of bloody diarrhea occurring up to seven times a day. His BMI had reduced from 22.9 kg/m² to 19.4 kg/m².\n\nPatient was pale, with bilateral lower abdominal tenderness but no peritonitis.\n\n- Laboratory tests: Routine laboratory tests were normal. Stool cultures were negative, and Clostridium difficile toxin was not present.- Imaging studies:  - Ultrasound: Showed mild thickening of the wall of the right colon  - CT: Abdominal CT was normal  - Endoscopy:  - Sigmoidoscopy showed continuous diffuse granular and friable mucosa to the ascending colon  - Biopsy findings: Moderately active colitis with cryptitis and crypt abscesses- Images:  Figure 1: Colonic biopsy samples  Description: (A) Colonic biopsy sample showing focal goblet cell depletion, acute and chronic inflammation in the lamina propria, cryptitis, and crypt abscesses  (B) Colonic mucosa sample without substantial changes taken at follow-up",
